message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an HTML “card” that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only CSS (no JavaScript) and works in modern browsers.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
body { margin: 0; padding: 0; display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center; height:100vh; background:#f0f0f0; font-family:sans-serif; }

/* Card container – keeps perspective so rotation looks 3‑D */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 800px;          /* gives depth to the 3‑D transform */
}

/* The actual card element */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth animation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* allow children to be positioned in 3‑D space */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%; height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;       /* hide backside while rotated */
    border-radius:10px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

/* Front styling */
.card .front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    text-align:center;
    padding:20px;
    color:#333;
}

/* Back styling – rotated 180° around Y axis */
.card .back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* start hidden behind front */
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    padding:20px;
    color:#555;
}

/* Hover effect – flip the card */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">
            <h2>Tytuł karty</h2>
            <p>To jest przykładowy opis frontu karty.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">
            <h3>Backside Title</h3>
            <p>Treść z tyłu karty pojawia się po obróceniu.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – `perspective` on `.card-wrapper` creates a 3‑D environment.
2. **Preserve‑3D** – `transform-style: preserve-3d` allows child elements (`.front`, `.back`) to maintain their 3‑D positions.
3. **Backface visibility** – `backface-visibility:hidden` hides the backside when it’s turned away from the viewer.
4. **Hover transform** – On hover, the whole `.card` rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back side.

Feel free to adjust colors, sizes, or add more content inside the `.front` and `.back` divs. Enjoy your rotating card!
